course: dictionary
lesson: 15847
title: The word undue
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Undue means more than is needed, right or sensible. It is another way of saying too much. Look at the words around it to find the clue. «We finished the job without undue delay.» Delay means waiting, so this means without too much waiting.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «We finished the job without too much delay» still makes sense, so you have worked it out. «Dad said there was no need for undue worry about the test.» Here undue tells you the worry is too much.
explain: Undue is a formal word. You will meet it in grown-up writing and school rules. «Please do not cause undue noise in the corridor.» The rule does not ban all noise, only noise that is too much. The clue is the word that comes just before it: noise.
fact: Undue means more than is needed, right or sensible; it is another way of saying too much.
fact: «Undue» is a formal word, used more in grown-up writing and school rules.
fact: The un- at the start is a clue that the word means not, as in «not sensible».
fact: Old use: undue can also mean not yet owed or due to be paid.
fact: «Undue stress» means more stress than is good for you.
exercise: «The teacher asked us not to make undue noise in the corridor.» What does undue mean here? | Noise made by the bell | Quiet noise, like a whisper | Noise that is needed | * Too much noise
exercise: What does «without undue delay» mean? | With a very long wait | * Without too much waiting | Before lunch | Without any job to do
exercise: Which word is a good swap for undue in «undue worry»? | Happy | Little | * Too much | Sleepy
test: «Dad said there was no need for undue worry about the test.» What does undue suggest? | No worry at all | * More worry than is sensible | Worry that is kind | Worry in the morning
test: In its old use, an undue bill is one that is... | Already paid for twice | Free to pay | * Not yet due to be paid | Lost in the post
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to undue? | Certain | * Excessive | Gentle | Shy
